Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.27,0:00:04.73,Episode Title,text,0,0,0,,{\3c&H6E6C70&\fad(446,429)\pos(490,322)}Episode 7 "You're So Close, I Think You May Make Me Dizzy"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.62,0:00:08.74,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Two months ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.10,0:00:13.18,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Lady Anastasia got into a carriage \Nrented by Baron Shaderan
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.18,0:00:15.24,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,and headed for Granado Castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.95,0:00:23.57,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,For a few days, she traveled in peace,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.22,0:00:27.17,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,then we're told that near the royal \Ncapital, she was set upon by bandits.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.34,0:00:32.79,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,While Lady Anastasia was \Ndesperately trying to escape...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.39,0:00:37.62,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,she fell into the river, which \Nhad swollen with the rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.76,0:00:41.68,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The driver tried to rescue her,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.68,0:00:44.61,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,but wounds inflicted by the \Nbandits made it impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.61,0:00:48.17,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The carriage was destroyed,\Nand everything it carried was stolen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.22,0:00:52.73,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,This summary of the incident is \Nbased on the driver's testimony
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.73,0:00:54.28,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,and the police investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.01,0:00:58.24,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Lady Anastasia's body hasn't been found,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.24,0:01:00.65,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,but they believe the chance \Nof her survival is dismal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.65,0:01:03.65,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,But the letter from her little brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.65,0:01:07.16,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,"Elder sister is already home."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.56,0:01:10.38,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,If Miss Anastasia is alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.38,0:01:13.62,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,won't Lady Marie try to distance \Nherself from Lord Kyros?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.98,0:01:17.86,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The master's love for her is good and true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.86,0:01:21.65,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Which means that it is necessary \Nfor someone to play the villain.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.65,0:01:25.52,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Y-You don't mean that you'll do \Nsomething to Miss Anastasia...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.68,0:01:26.59,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.59,0:01:29.75,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The master has forbidden me \Nfrom using violent methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.75,0:01:31.96,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I won't do anything extreme. \NWell, not overly so.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.96,0:01:35.31,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Wh-What does "not overly so" \Nmean? Can I just go home now?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.62,0:01:38.39,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,"Companions enrich a journey" \Nis a favorite proverb of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:41.19,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.77,0:01:45.80,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,it's possible that more than just \Nsnakes will dart from the underbrush.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.64,0:03:19.84,Narration,Marie; narration,0,0,0,,A few days after Mio left...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.46,0:03:27.99,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, starting today, I'll be your \Nattendant. I look forward to serving.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.99,0:03:29.03,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.03,0:03:33.00,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Oh. As you might expect, the maid \Nuniforms aren't sized to fit me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.00,0:03:34.90,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Th-That wasn't my concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.10,0:03:39.28,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,A lady's maid is relied upon in an \Nemotional sense as well, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.28,0:03:40.66,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.66,0:03:45.05,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,We do spend a lot of time together, so \Nit is easy to feel rather close to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.05,0:03:45.82,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.23,0:03:49.53,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, I want to become the \Nperson you get along with best.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.53,0:03:51.55,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,That's why I decided to \Nbecome your attendant.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.43,0:03:57.35,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,His eyes are so clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.82,0:04:06.24,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,What do you think? Well done \Nfor my first time, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.24,0:04:09.02,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.32,0:04:12.08,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,All right. Next is your dress, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.08,0:04:14.83,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,What? He can't mean that he'll dress me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.83,0:04:16.69,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I couldn't endure that! I'll die!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.25,0:04:20.40,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,What do you say? If you don't have \Na particular one in mind, I'll—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.40,0:04:22.86,Default,Cillie,0,0,0,,You broke your promise!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.31,0:04:26.57,Default,Cillie,0,0,0,,I said I'd dress her, didn't I?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.57,0:04:28.78,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Th-That's no reason to come flying at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.78,0:04:32.70,Default,Cillie,0,0,0,,Master, you just want to touch \NMarie, don't you? You lecher!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.54,0:04:36.18,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,Cillie has been quite disrespectful.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.18,0:04:38.72,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,However, Master, the closeness \Nthat makes you happy
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.96,0:04:42.40,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,seems to be a level of closeness \Nthat makes Lady Marie nervous.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.40,0:04:44.27,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,One should temper one's eagerness.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.47,0:04:50.18,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\fad(484,1)\shad0\fs30\fnTimes New Roman\pos(318,245)\c&H475E61&\3c&HDBF1F7&}The Next Day
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.84,0:04:52.63,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, let's go on a date!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.88,0:04:55.70,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.44,0:04:59.51,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,This morning, a letter arrived from Luiphon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.51,0:05:04.05,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,He writes, "I've prepared a tremendous gift \Nfor you, so please come to the royal capital."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.69,0:05:08.16,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\fad(447,1)\fnArial\fs15\shad0\frz15.56\pos(283,175)\c&H161817&\3c&HE0FDFA&}Third Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.05,0:05:06.96,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Though, knowing him,\NI wouldn't expect too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.65,0:05:10.44,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,And so...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.44,0:05:13.65,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Will you go out with me? Just the two of us?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.01,0:05:17.08,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.03,0:05:30.98,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Those kind of clothes are \Nnice, too. You look lovely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.98,0:05:34.70,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lord Kyros.\NYou look wonderful as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.70,0:05:35.80,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.13,0:05:39.50,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,But if you talk like that, \Npeople will find out who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.50,0:05:42.12,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Call me just "Kyros," with no title.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.12,0:05:43.56,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What? What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.91,0:05:46.54,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,There's still time before our \Nappointment with Luiphon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.54,0:05:49.50,Default,Myros,0,0,0,,Let's go look around at everything first.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.90,0:05:56.59,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,If we get separated or lost, then this rare \Nchance at a date will be ruined, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.71,0:06:04.81,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Th-Then, shall—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.47,0:06:08.35,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Let's go, Kyros.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.81,0:06:18.39,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,This is where Lady Marie is from?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.39,0:06:21.61,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,In the Shaderan lands, aside from \Nlargely wheat-based farming,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.61,0:06:24.61,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,raising cattle makes up the \Nmajority of the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.95,0:06:30.19,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Really? I'd heard they were poor, \Nso I imagined a small, dried-up village.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.19,0:06:31.55,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,It's good land.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.55,0:06:36.25,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,However, after the war, taxes were \Nlevied according to a region's size,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.25,0:06:39.37,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,so they've had to continue \Ncultivating large swathes of land.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.85,0:06:43.27,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Maintaining the land and rotation \Nof use is a lord's job,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.27,0:06:45.38,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,but it doesn't appear to be done well here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.77,0:06:54.83,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Um, where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.83,0:06:56.59,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Lady Marie's old school.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.59,0:06:57.32,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.58,0:07:02.81,Default,receptionist,0,0,0,,I haven't seen you before. \NAre you a new student?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.10,0:07:07.51,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Well, I came from the royal capital \Nto learn about farming, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.31,0:07:11.66,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,And I was thinking that I'd like \Nto ask the students here about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.66,0:07:13.70,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Are there any girls here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.70,0:07:18.70,Default,receptionist,0,0,0,,Well, up until last year, the daughter of \NBaron Shaderan attended our school, but now...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.93,0:07:22.16,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Oh my! A baron's daughter? \NI couldn't possibly!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.16,0:07:25.67,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Isn't there anyone who's graduated \Nthat I could speak to more casually?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.67,0:07:29.14,Default,receptionist,0,0,0,,I believe the daughter of the \Nlocal innkeeper also attended,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.14,0:07:32.68,Default,receptionist,0,0,0,,but she found work in the royal \Ncapital, and withdrew mid-term.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.97,0:07:35.35,Default,receptionist,0,0,0,,I think her name was Karina.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.77,0:07:38.15,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,That serves my purposes quite nicely.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.58,0:07:42.05,Default,Mrs. Burton,0,0,0,,Yes? May I ask who you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.50,0:07:45.02,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,You are Karina Burton's mother, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.02,0:07:47.09,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I am a detective from the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.93,0:07:52.58,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The truth is, your daughter may have \Ngotten caught up in a certain incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.58,0:07:53.31,Default,Mrs. Burton,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.54,0:07:58.22,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I need to check your daughter's student \Nidentification from when she attended school.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.22,0:08:00.22,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,If possible, I'd like to \Nborrow it for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.83,0:08:05.53,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Th-There should be limits to this nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.03,0:08:08.07,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I didn't lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.07,0:08:11.79,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Unlike the police, being a detective is a \Njob where calling yourself one makes you one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.79,0:08:14.23,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,But you talked about some kind of incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.23,0:08:17.63,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,A baron's daughter, thought to have died \Nin an accident, may still be alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.63,0:08:19.15,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,That's quite the incident, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.15,0:08:22.82,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,And the possibility that Karina \NBurton is involved isn't zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.82,0:08:25.56,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,You're being reckless, Miss Mio.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.02,0:08:27.83,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Please don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.83,0:08:30.31,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The big lies begin now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.31,0:08:31.98,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,No! You're scaring me!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.72,0:08:37.99,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The Shaderan residence is just over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.99,0:08:40.34,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Please be careful not to \Nexpose your background.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.34,0:08:43.11,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Um, shouldn't we discuss \Nthis before we do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.11,0:08:45.39,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Please adapt as we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.35,0:08:49.98,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I'll just keep quiet the whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.97,0:08:56.34,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,This is an impressive mansion!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.59,0:09:00.63,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Yes, it is. However, it isn't \Nbeing managed very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.03,0:09:03.64,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,It wasn't this bad previously, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.17,0:09:10.89,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Miss Mio?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.82,0:09:14.29,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Hey! Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.69,0:09:16.74,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,If you're tradesmen, go around the back!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.74,0:09:19.32,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,You aren't debt collectors, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.65,0:09:23.05,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I'm Karina! This is my fiancé, Henry!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.05,0:09:26.36,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,This is my friend's house, and when we \Narrived, the gate was open, so we came in!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.36,0:09:27.29,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.57,0:09:28.50,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.50,0:09:31.66,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I just told you! I'm dear Marie's friend!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.76,0:09:35.80,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,A friend? Of that raggedy girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.18,0:09:41.46,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I met Marie in the capital! We went to \Nthe same school, so we became friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.46,0:09:45.30,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,It's true, that girl is supposedly \Nat the capital right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.30,0:09:47.68,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,When I said I'd be visiting home,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.68,0:09:51.19,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,she asked me if I'd come and \Npick up something she'd wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.89,0:09:55.65,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Miss, will you let me \Ninto dear Marie's room?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.34,0:10:01.63,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Make sure you leave as soon as you're done.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.07,0:10:11.41,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.93,0:10:17.95,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,That girl was never good at the basics.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.95,0:10:21.17,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Cooking and cleaning took her so \Nlong she never really finished,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.17,0:10:23.43,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,so she started sleeping here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.97,0:10:27.39,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Why did Marie have to work so hard?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.39,0:10:29.69,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Because she wasn't the least bit cute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.92,0:10:33.27,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,A woman with no prospect \Nof marriage has to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.27,0:10:36.87,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Then, when did she stop being cute?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.87,0:10:39.24,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,She's been like that since she was born!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.24,0:10:43.80,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Compared with Lady Anastasia, she's \Nimpertinent and completely unlovable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.80,0:10:47.86,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,Her grandmother, Lady Sasha, was the one \Nperson who showed her some affection.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.21,0:10:49.47,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Sasha...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.05,0:10:52.74,Default,Cedric,0,0,0,,Big Sis Marie?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.18,0:10:56.62,Default,Cedric,0,0,0,,H-Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.62,0:10:57.91,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Cedric!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.91,0:10:59.48,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.66,0:11:04.38,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Who are you two?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.23,0:11:07.11,Italics,Tomas; internal,0,0,0,,Baron Shaderan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.77,0:11:10.90,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Pleased to meet you! I'm Karina Burton!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.90,0:11:12.44,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Dear Marie is my friend!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.06,0:11:19.76,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,I now understand what brought \Nthe two of you here, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.82,0:11:24.00,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,That Tania! She loves her jokes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.40,0:11:26.61,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,This is a storage shed, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.61,0:11:30.09,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,It couldn't possibly be \Nmy darling Marie's room.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.09,0:11:30.67,Default,Tania,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.18,0:11:33.72,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,I'll show you to the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.72,0:11:34.72,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Cedric!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.98,0:11:37.58,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,You go back to your room \Nand continue your studies!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.58,0:11:39.02,Default,Cedric,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.90,0:11:43.44,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,This is the first time a friend \Nof Marie's has visited us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.09,0:11:47.99,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,She's a bookworm, and so shy. \NDon't you find her a bit gloomy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.53,0:11:53.44,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,What? Marie is so cheerful and \Nkind, everyone loves her!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.17,0:11:57.40,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,I see. As her father, \NI'm happy to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.78,0:12:00.86,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,By the way, what is it that \Nyou've come to pick up?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.05,0:12:05.15,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,It's something precious to \Na girl, so it's a secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.15,0:12:07.56,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,She asked me to look for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.65,0:12:13.16,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Go right in. This is Marie's room.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.93,0:12:18.75,Italics,Tomas; internal,0,0,0,,What? So she did have a \Nproper room after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.75,0:12:20.81,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Oh, are you playing tricks on us too, Baron?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.81,0:12:22.85,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,This is her sister's room, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.20,0:12:26.67,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,What makes you think that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.67,0:12:28.88,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Dear Marie loves to study.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.88,0:12:31.46,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,It'd be odd if her room didn't \Nhave bookshelves in it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.46,0:12:32.64,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.28,0:12:37.86,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Now, stop playing silly \Npranks. You can't trick me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.19,0:12:43.69,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Sorry about that! I really will \Nshow you the way this time!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.11,0:12:47.66,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Here. This is Marie's room.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.66,0:12:51.20,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,I'll leave, so search as much as you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.20,0:12:58.58,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Is this really Lady Marie's room?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.23,0:13:02.14,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.69,0:13:05.11,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Wait! What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.11,0:13:06.46,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Shh! Quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.46,0:13:10.09,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,Really? I'm so glad to hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.62,0:13:12.87,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The wife's room seems \Nto be next to this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.87,0:13:13.82,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.94,0:13:17.42,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,That's so true, Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.64,0:13:26.37,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,My dear guests, I'm so sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.37,0:13:29.55,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,We're supposed to go out \Nas a family, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.55,0:13:31.29,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Can I ask you to leave for today?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.97,0:13:36.51,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Oh, really? Well then,\Nwe'll excuse ourselves here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.04,0:13:40.32,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Oh, and when you get back, \Ncould you tell Marie something for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.32,0:13:43.96,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,If there's something she wants, she \Nshould come back and get it herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.20,0:13:48.16,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,That's so true! But dear Marie seems so busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.16,0:13:52.17,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,After all, there's only a month left until \Nher betrothal ceremony to the count!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.17,0:13:54.34,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,That may be true...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.65,0:13:57.89,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,but if the ceremony hasn't happened, \Nthen she isn't engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.89,0:14:02.27,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,That girl still belongs to me,\Nand I'm not letting anyone steal her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.64,0:14:06.75,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Then, Marie must be very important to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.44,0:14:08.83,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,I suppose so.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.83,0:14:09.87,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,Oh my.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.25,0:14:14.28,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,We have guests? I'll go and \Nprepare some tea right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.28,0:14:18.92,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,No, they were just leaving. \NAnd we're all going out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.92,0:14:21.81,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,Really? Then if you'll wait just a moment...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.72,0:14:25.92,Italics,Tomas; internal,0,0,0,,That's Lady Marie's mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.92,0:14:28.01,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,Mama's going out now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.01,0:14:30.59,Default,Elvira,0,0,0,,Be a good girl and wait, \Nwon't you, Anastasia?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.98,0:14:42.37,Default,Gregor,0,0,0,,Well, enjoy your visit home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.37,0:14:44.17,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I will! If you'll excuse us.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.69,0:14:50.79,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I broke out in a cold sweat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.79,0:14:53.12,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,We'll wait a bit, then return to the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.12,0:14:53.78,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.09,0:14:59.99,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Ow.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.28,0:15:02.75,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,We're lucky that they didn't lock up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.75,0:15:05.45,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Now, come before the maid notices.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.28,0:15:09.89,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,M-Miss Mio, you are a maid, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.89,0:15:12.33,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I am, without question, a maid. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.87,0:15:25.16,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,So you did survive... Lady Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.60,0:15:43.58,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,A-A doll?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.95,0:15:59.42,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Do you think that the shock of losing Miss \NAnastasia drove Baroness Elvira insane?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.42,0:16:01.63,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,No, she's sane.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.63,0:16:04.73,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,She understands that it's just a doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.28,0:16:10.35,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,It was made very recently. \NMost likely by the baroness herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.35,0:16:13.35,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,But it looks so much like a real person.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.74,0:16:16.33,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Well, the hair was real human hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.33,0:16:17.28,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Human hair?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.54,0:16:19.05,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,And the dress, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.05,0:16:21.84,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Using the police \Ninvestigations as reference,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.84,0:16:25.16,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,there's no doubt she was wearing\N that dress during the accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.16,0:16:30.88,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,W-Wait. Miss Anastasia fell into the \Nriver and her body wasn't found, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.22,0:16:33.17,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Then how did her hair and clothes...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.17,0:16:38.00,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Indeed. There are inconsistencies with the \Nevents of the accident as we know them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.88,0:16:40.35,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,And if that's the case...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.65,0:16:45.85,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Please return us immediately.\NThere is someone I must meet with.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.85,0:16:47.12,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Do you mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.79,0:16:51.99,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,The driver of the hired carriage... is lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.38,0:16:58.93,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Delicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.93,0:17:00.99,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,So these are the flavors of Ipsandros.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.26,0:17:03.63,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I often came here while I was a student.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.63,0:17:06.10,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,The food in the dormitory \Nwas all too refined.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.10,0:17:09.21,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,You attended the Royal Academy just \Nlike Prince Luiphon, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.21,0:17:09.88,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.45,0:17:14.55,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,From the age of twelve to the age of \Neighteen, I attended and learned many things.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.55,0:17:16.76,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,What a strange sort of feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.47,0:17:20.68,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Lord Kyros was a young child once, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.36,0:17:24.40,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,All right. For dessert, we'll have dondurma!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.40,0:17:28.78,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Dondurma? In Ipsian, that means \N"a frozen thing," doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.57,0:17:31.73,Default,stall owner,0,0,0,,Here you go!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.37,0:17:36.17,Default,stall owner,0,0,0,,There you go! Enjoy!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.17,0:17:37.33,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.49,0:17:40.26,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.49,0:17:40.94,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.27,0:17:43.17,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Wait! Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.45,0:17:44.91,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\fad(321,1)\an8\shad0\fnArial\fs24\c&H8181D0&\3c&H4779AC&\bord0.51\b1}PRECIOUS...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.54,0:17:44.91,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Please don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.91,0:17:47.02,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Honestly! Please control yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.02,0:17:48.29,Default,stall owner,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.33,0:17:52.34,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Oh, it's chewy! It's quite delicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.64,0:17:54.54,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Kyros, would you like to have some... too?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.54,0:17:57.99,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Th-The cuteness is too much. It's killing me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.99,0:17:59.42,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Honestly!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.14,0:18:09.57,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Th-This is incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.57,0:18:12.75,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,This shop handles goods from every country.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.75,0:18:15.56,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Foreign goods are popular \Namong merchants, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.56,0:18:19.11,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Once you've tried Ips silk undergarments, \Nyou'll never be able to wear any others.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.53,0:18:23.45,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,You said that the first time we met, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.82,0:18:28.42,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Say, Kyros, will you allow me to buy \None thing for you as a present?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.81,0:18:35.36,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Lady Liu Liu paid me for helping with \Nwriting letters and translating.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.36,0:18:37.22,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,So if there's anything you'd like—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.77,0:18:43.05,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Well, that's a top-quality, one-of-a-kind \Nimported item, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.28,0:18:45.91,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I-I didn't realize these were so costly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.48,0:18:50.53,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, does this suit me?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.53,0:18:55.44,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, it does. But I think the fancier \None there would suit you well, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.94,0:18:57.69,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Right then!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.69,0:19:00.00,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I'd like to try on the ones \Nthat Marie mentioned!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.00,0:19:01.75,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,All of them! I'll buy them all!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.75,0:19:02.70,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.28,0:19:10.27,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.27,0:19:11.32,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,How wonderful!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.34,0:19:21.34,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad0\fs20\fnGeorgia\b1\c&HD8FBFC&\3c&H3B7380&\bord1.5\pos(146,22)}Flarian\N{\fs15}student uniform
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.92,0:19:24.83,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,A student uniform? Where will you wear it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.83,0:19:28.32,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I'll wear it to cheer you \Nup when you're down, Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.32,0:19:29.91,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Right! I'll buy this, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.91,0:19:31.07,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.52,0:19:39.23,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,It will probably still take a little \Nwhile for him to finish changing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.68,0:19:47.53,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,These are priced at a bargain.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.25,0:19:52.08,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,This would be perfect for Lord Kyros!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.83,0:19:58.83,Default,Mysterious voice,0,0,0,,Marie?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.58,0:20:02.32,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.03,0:20:05.05,Default,man,0,0,0,,Hey there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.51,0:20:07.56,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,What? Did I mishear before?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.56,0:20:09.43,Default,man,0,0,0,,Miss, are you here alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.43,0:20:11.55,Default,man,0,0,0,,How about a café if you haven't eaten?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.00,0:20:14.17,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Is he trying to get customers?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.86,0:20:17.78,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I've already eaten.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.06,0:20:20.75,Default,man,0,0,0,,Then, just some tea! My treat!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.75,0:20:22.56,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.92,0:20:25.08,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I don't need tea. Please let go of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.17,0:20:28.07,Default,man,0,0,0,,You are cute, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.62,0:20:31.22,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,He's forcing himself to \Ncompliment me out of courtesy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.22,0:20:32.95,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I should express my gratitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.95,0:20:34.74,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Oh, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.74,0:20:36.58,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I don't want to!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.86,0:20:39.09,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Help me, Lord Kyros!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.75,0:20:46.71,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,What an unmannerly way to hit on someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.10,0:20:49.45,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,When a lady says no, walk away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.45,0:20:51.36,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Don't touch anyone without \Ntheir permission!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.36,0:20:54.07,Default,man,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.50,0:21:00.82,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I'm sorry for causing trouble for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.82,0:21:02.73,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,You have absolutely no reason to apologize!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.04,0:21:05.85,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,But... didn't you realize that \Nhe was trying to ask you out?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.85,0:21:06.44,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.82,0:21:08.95,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,It must have happened \Nmany times before this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.95,0:21:12.78,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,N-No. My school was almost all boys,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.66,0:21:15.98,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,but they never spoke to me more \Nthan absolutely necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.52,0:21:19.37,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,They used to point at me and laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.58,0:21:21.08,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,That's not possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.08,0:21:26.10,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Even unadorned, you're so charming \Nthat men would never leave you alone!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.32,0:21:32.06,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I'm not. I'm ugly, and my hair \Nand clothes are always raggedy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.06,0:21:33.64,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,Raggedy...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.05,0:21:37.45,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,That's it! That's why they \Nkept her in tatters!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.45,0:21:40.78,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,Baron Shaderan didn't want Marie's \Ncharms known to anyone...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.78,0:21:43.68,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,No! He wished to conceal it, even from her,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.68,0:21:45.95,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,so he trapped her in that disgraceful state!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.29,0:21:50.44,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,But... no matter how hard he tries \Nto tie Marie down, it won't work!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.08,0:21:57.87,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I'm never letting go.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.85,0:22:06.55,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Unlike those of other people, \NLord Kyros' hand is comforting.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.60,0:24:03.21,Default,Cillie,0,0,0,,It's so {\i1}lonely{\i0} without Marie here!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.21,0:24:07.00,Default Top,Cillie,0,0,0,,Stupid Master! It's {\i1}no fair!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.10,0:24:08.01,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,Now, now, Cillie.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.45,0:24:12.59,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,Still, they are quite late \Nin returning, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.18,0:24:15.51,Default,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,I hope nothing has happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.08,0:24:17.31,Default Top,Cillie,0,0,0,,Next time...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.31,0:24:19.68,Default Top,Cillie,0,0,0,,"A Gift More Lovely Than Jewels."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.39,0:24:27.01,Episode Title,text,0,0,0,,{\3c&H2B4569&\fad(438,1)\pos(504,320)}Episode 8 "A \NGift More Lovely Than Jewels"
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.24,0:24:22.42,Default Top,Cillie,0,0,0,,If you don't watch, I'll send \Nyou flying with a kick!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.42,0:24:23.63,Default Top,Wolfgang,0,0,0,,Now, Cillie!
